On Thursday, December 6, 2012 7:07:17 PM UTC-5, Ben Goodrich wrote:
> On Thursday, December 6, 2012 4:48:45 PM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> > In:
> >
> >      http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/boost/utility/result_of.hpp
> >
> > there's a code comment (and supporting #defines);
> >
> >      // Use the decltype-based version of result_of by default if the compiler
> >      // supports N3276 <http://www.open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2011/n3276.pdf>.
> >      // The user can force the choice by defining either BOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_DECLTYPE or
> >      // BOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_TR1, but not both!
> >
> > I changed the CFLAGS in the top-level stan/makefile:
> >
> >      CFLAGS = -I src -I $(EIGEN) -I $(BOOST) -O$O -Wall -DBOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_TR1 -DBOOST_NO_DECLTYPE
> >
> > Will this work on Windows or do we need to do something different?
>
> Still broken with clang++-3.1 and O=3 (log attached), but now the failures are similar to those of g++-4.7.

