From u2a7f346506a3e9ff at groups.google.com  Fri Dec  7 22:49:50 2012
From: u2a7f346506a3e9ff at groups.google.com (Marcus Brubaker)
Date: Fri, 07 Dec 2012 22:49:50 +0000
Subject: Explicit integration with RMHMC
Message-ID: <uEpGchIASZE.VaXeDXLQXFsJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/uEpGchIASZE/m/VaXeDXLQXFsJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I thought some people here might be interested in this:

http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.3759

Girolami and others have come up with a way to perform Riemann Manifold HMC with an explicit integration method, making it much more efficient.  I haven't gone through it in detail yet, but it looks very promising and the trick they use to do it is very simple but fairly clever, ie, changing from Hamiltonian dynamics to Lagrangian dynamics.

Cheers,
Marcus

