> Now std::forward seems to be built into C++, so why isn't Eigen
> finding it?  We certainly don't use it on our own anywhere.

This link

http://marshall.calepin.co/llvmclang-and-standard-libraries-on-mac-os-x.html

seems to have the best explanation among the hits I got from Google. And it raises yet another issue: Should we be adding

CFLAGS += -stdlib=libc++

when Clang is used to use Clang's version of the standard C++ library rather than g++'s? I think so, even though it is less widely used. This

http://libcxx.llvm.org/

claims that it is "a 100% complete C++11 implementation on Apple's OS X" and it works for me on Debian. It probably doesn't work on Windows but just getting clang++ to work on Windows requires a few steps (that we haven't attempted yet).

Ben

