I think the problem with the parser test was that
the includes were for the _def.hpp with the definitions
rather than just the headers in the .hpp files.

The size issues were probably due to the double definitions.

The current makefile does NOT use any c++11 features
for g++ or clang++ in the os_mac config.  For clang++,
Daniel even included warnings for c++11 extensions.

With the current makefile, tests pass for me on
Mac OS X Lion, with latest Xcode versions of g++
and clang++ at -O0 and -O3 optimization:

~/stan>clang++ --version

Apple clang version 4.1 (tags/Apple/clang-421.11.66) (based on LLVM 3.1svn)

~/stan>g++ --version
i686-apple-darwin11-llvm-g++-4.2 (GCC) 4.2.1 (Based on Apple Inc. build 5658) (LLVM build 2336.11.00)

Before the change they passed with g++ -O0, but not g++ -O3.
I'm not sure why it would've worked with -O0 given the double definitions.

I'm wondering if the ';' vs ',' in the strings output is
just a change in arbitrary convention rather than something
important.

I'll try to install clang++ 3.2 and g++ 4.7 version and see if I can
get it working.

- Bob

