That would be fine, but the wall time for the model tests currently is not that useful because it includes compile time in addition to execution time and also starts with clock seeds, which can introduce a lot of variability. I have mostly been looking for evidence of speed differences by sourcing rstan/example/demo.R in R. That has a little bit of overhead from RStan but resolves the limitations of test-models for this purpose. However, I've only done that for various configurations on my laptop, so I don't know about other OSes.

