I think the issue here is not that we're going to say Stan won't work somewhere, but that we only have so much time and so many resources to try to certify compatibility with a whole raft of configurations.

To put it another way, maybe the thing to say is "we think Stan should work on any sufficiently modern, standards compliant platform that Boost and Eigen also support, however we will only check and block releases on the following platforms/configurations: ..."

That list can grow or shrink as resources become available or obvious gaps appear and we obviously want to make it work on as many platforms as possible, but we can't possible test and/or block on all of them.

