>
> That list can grow or shrink as resources become available or obvious gaps appear and we obviously want to make it work on as many platforms as possible, but we can't possible test and/or block on all of them.

That is what I mean. I just think the distinction between supported and unsupported is murky. There are 1) configurations that passed test-unit at some known point, 2) configurations that failed at some known point, 3) configurations that we are not aware of ever being tested, and 4) configurations for which we wouldn't release Stan unless test-unit passed. I'm fine with saying that 4) are the supported configurations, but I think we should say that the complement of 4) is unsupported without emphasizing that unsupported configurations often work as illustrated by 1). And we should try to keep the wiki as up-to-date as possible about 1), 2), and 3).

Ben

