These problems you're seeing look a lot like the behavior we had in Windows a while back where a bin/stanc was being built improperly without any compiler warnings.

If you are seeing those messages, then bin/stanc isn't being built properly. We should track down which compiler flag combinations don't work for the compiler versions.

I found out the hard way that adding an std flag to g++ actually affects the compiler's behavior with respect to memory boundaries.

