want to run the model and then see if we get the right kind
of exception reported.  If we run the executable that gets
compiled, we can look for strings in the output.  Maybe we
could check return codes -- I don't know what that is for
an uncaught formatting exception.

The alternative would be to try to run the model in a test
that expects the right kind of exception (that is, don't
run it as a command, but from within the test framework).

